  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Bidding**: Forehand determines trump or everyone bids for special contracts. 2. **Marriages**: King and Queen of the same suit score bonus points (40 for trump, 20 for others) when one is led. 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. If unable to follow suit, players MUST play a trump (Stechzwang). 4. **Counting**: Ace=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2. Total in deck is 120 points.',
    Player: '1. **Bidding**: Forehand determines trump or everyone bids for special contracts. 2. **Marriages**: King and Queen of the same suit score bonus points (40 for trump, 20 for others) when one is led. 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. If unable to follow suit, players MUST play a trump (Stechzwang). 4. **Counting**: Ace=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2. Total in deck is 120 points.',
    objective: 'Score 66 points in a deal to win the round, or satisfy a higher bid contract. First team to reach 24 game points (counting down) wins the session.',
    gameplay: '1. **Bidding**: Forehand determines trump or everyone bids for special contracts. 2. **Marriages**: King and Queen of the same suit score bonus points (40 for trump, 20 for others) when one is led. 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. If unable to follow suit, players MUST play a trump (Stechzwang). 4. **Counting**: Ace=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2. Total in deck is 120 points.',
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible.',
      'Must trump if void in the led suit (Stechzwang).',
      'Winning the last trick scores no extra points, but provides the final tally.',
      'If a team reaches 66 points, they stop the game immediately.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players in two fixed partnerships; partners sit opposite each other.',
      deck: '20 cards. Ranks: Ace (11), 10 (10), King (4), Queen (Ober, 3), Jack (Unter, 2) in four suits.',
      equipment: 'Standard 20-card deck (French or German suited), score sheet.',
      dealing: 'Dealer deals 3 cards to each player. Forehand (left of dealer) calls trump or knocks. Then 2 more cards are dealt to each player.',
